 # でこぼこ — uneven and bumpy
 
 ## Meaning
 
-An uneven arrangement of raised and sunken parts. 凸凹 is a dictionary spelling of でこぼこ. It also describes an imbalance or mismatch, such as people of markedly different heights.
+An uneven arrangement of raised and sunken parts. [凸](../kanji/凸.md)[凹](../kanji/凹.md) is a dictionary spelling of でこぼこ: 凸 is the raised part and 凹 the sunken part. It also describes an imbalance or mismatch, such as people of markedly different heights.
 
 - この道はでこぼこしていて、自転車で走りにくい。 — This road is bumpy and hard to cycle along.
 - パテで壁（かべ）のでこぼこを埋めた（うめた）。 — I filled the uneven spots in the wall with putty.
 - 背の高い兄と小さい弟は、でこぼこコンビだ。 — The tall older brother and small younger brother make a mismatched pair.
 
